3. Why I recommend GenerateRequest

This is important.

Suppose Power Apps creates:

ID 101 → GNS-202610-0097 → B014172
ID 102 → GNS-202610-0097 → B012504
ID 103 → GNS-202610-0097 → B019999

Power Automate's:

When an item is created

can trigger three times.

If ID 101 triggers first, Power Automate might query SharePoint before IDs 102 and 103 have been created.

It could see only:

B014172

and generate an incomplete document.

Therefore, the best solution is:

Power Apps creates all user records
              ↓
Power Apps marks ONE record
GenerateRequest = Yes
              ↓
Power Automate starts generation
              ↓
Get ALL records for ReferenceNo

This is much safer than relying on a delay.


