19. Important — sanitize ReferenceNo

This is something I recommend adding.

Some characters aren't allowed in SharePoint filenames.

For example:

/
\
:
*
?
"
<
>
|

If your ReferenceNo is always something like:

GNS-202610-0097

you don't have a problem.

But if ReferenceNo might contain /, create a Compose:

SafeReferenceNo

Expression:

replace(
    replace(
        replace(
            triggerBody()?['ReferenceNo'],
            '/',
            '-'
        ),
        '\',
        '-'
    ),
    ':',
    '-'
)

Then use:

Reactivation-@{outputs('SafeReferenceNo')}.xlsx

If your ReferenceNo format is always GNS-YYYYMM-NNNN, you can simply use ReferenceNo directly.


